"""User interface: buttons, DIP switch, buzzer and LEDs.

Buttons (GT-TC048B tactile switches, MCU internal pull-ups), as on the v1 main board:
- SW2 on Button (PC4) with C20 100 nF to GND.
- SW3 on NRST with C21 100 nF to GND, the recommended NRST protection (DS13311 Figure 27
  p168: 0.1 uF; the pin has an internal 30-50 kOhm pull-up, Table 61 p167). The ESP32 also
  drives NRST, open drain (ESP sheet), and so does an ST-Link's RST wire on SWD1 pad 1 (root
  sheet).
BOOT0: R42 10 kOhm (AN5419 Figure 19 p30) and C60 100 nF to GND hold it low, so the MCU always
boots from flash; there is no BOOT0 button.
SW1, a 4-way DIP switch, pulls Switch_0..3 to GND (Switch_0 on PH0, Switch_1-3 on PH1, PC15, PC14,
all with the MCU's internal pull-ups).

Buzzer: BZ1 (FUET-5025, 3 V electromagnetic, externally driven) from 3V3_D through R3 10 Ohm to
the low-side switch Q1 (AO3400A), driven from Buzzer (PB9, TIM17) through R1 220 Ohm with R2
10 kOhm gate pull-down; D3 (1N4148WS) clamps the coil: at most
the 174 mA coil current below, decaying, against its 300 mA IFM and 2 A IFSM at 1 us. R3 is a 1206 (250 mW): at the firmware's
50 % duty and low tones the coil current approaches 3.3 V / (9 + 10) Ohm = 174 mA with the 9 Ohm
minimum coil (FUET-5025 p2), 151 mW in R3.

LEDs:
- D1, D2: CHONGTIAN CT-1515UGRBC/H-P9-MX4 addressable LEDs (1.5 x 1.5 mm) in a chain on 3V3_D
  (research IR emitters and status LEDs; A.4), replacing the v1 main board's WS2815C-2020, whose
  9.5-13.5 V supply range fits neither 4S nor 3.3 V. DI of D1 on LED_ARGB (PA2, TIM15_CH1), D1 DO to
  D2 DI. JLCPCB places it with Economic PCBA; the Worldsemi WS2812C-2427-V6 and -2020-V6 (rated
  from 3.3 V), the WS2812B-2020-V6 and -MINI-V6, the XL-2121RGBC-2812B and the TCWIN T64/T65/T77 are
  Standard PCBA only (JLCPCB's order page, 2026-11-08), and of the parts it places for Economic the
  SK6805D-EC2018 needs 3.7 V, the CT-3227 emits sideways and the WS2816A-1313's 5-pad land is drawn
  0.05 mm apart, under JLCPCB's 0.1 mm. VDD 3-7.5 V in the recommended operating range (CT-1515
  datasheet A2 p3-4; its electrical tables are at 4.5-5.0 V, and p1 calls it "100 %" from 5 V up), DI
  VIH 0.7 x VDD, 2.30-2.35 V on this rail, and VIL 0.3 x VDD, 0.99 V (p4), so PA2 (VOH >= VDD - 0.4
  V, VOL <= 0.4 V, DS13311 Table 56) drives it directly with 0.53 V and 0.59 V of margin; C19 (D1)
  and C18 (D2) 100 nF on VDD (p7: a capacitor per LED, value not given). Its bit timing holds the
  high times to T0H 0.295 us and T1H 0.595 us +-0.05 us, low times under 20 us and a bit of at least
  1.2 us, reset >= 80 us (p6), against the WS2815C's 5 us (boards/main/firmware_changes.toml, leds).
  3.3 V operation: 3.3 V is inside the operating range but below the tables' 4.5 V, and the
  datasheet draws no sink headroom curve. Each channel sinks a constant 5 mA (4-6 mA, p4); like any
  constant-current sink it keeps its current while VDD exceeds the LED's VF by the sink's drop. A
  comparable InGaN RGB part reads 2.76 V blue and 2.88 V green at 5 mA (Everlight EAST1616RGBA4 Rev
  1, Figures p7-8, typical), leaving 0.4-0.5 V at the rail's 3.284 V minimum: red keeps full current
  and green and blue may sit at the sink's knee, dimmer; the colours stay recognisable, and the
  status LEDs run far below full brightness anyway.
- D5 (red) from 3V3_D through R5 1 kOhm, the power indicator: (3.3 V - VF) / 1 kOhm is
  0.9-1.5 mA for the KT-0603R's VF 1.8-2.4 V (LCSC C2286 listing, at its rated current; VF is
  lower at 1 mA), a faint indicator at a twentieth of its 20 mA rating (the owner, 2026-11-10: a
  little dimmer than 680 Ohm's 1.3-2.2 mA).
- D4 (blue, KENTO KT-0603B datasheet, LCSC C2288, p3 sections 4-5: VF 2.6-3.1 V and IV
  70-175 mcd at IF = 5 mA, IF 30 mA DC max) from LED_Blue (PB2; LED_Red in the v1 firmware,
  firmware_changes.toml leds) through R4 1 kOhm, R5's value: the owner asks the blue to match the
  red (2026-11-10). Light is about proportional to IF at low current, so the bins' slopes are
  14-35 mcd/mA for D4 (70-175 mcd at 5 mA) and 15 mcd/mA for D5 (300 mcd at 20 mA, C2286
  listing), whose 0.9-1.5 mA give it 14-23 mcd. The datasheet draws no IF-VF curve; a comparable
  InGaN 0603 blue rises about 0.3 V from 0 to 10 mA (Everlight 19-217/BHC-ZL1M2RY/6T DSE-0014124
  Rev 5 p5, Forward Current vs. Forward Voltage, typical), so near 1 mA a die sits about 0.2 V under
  its 5 mA VF: a mid-bin 2.85 V part at about 2.65 V draws (3.3 - 2.65) / 1 kOhm = 0.65 mA, 9-23
  mcd, the red's brightness. PB2's high level is VDD - 0.4 V at 8 mA (DS13311 Table 56): at most
  0.4 V / 8 mA = 50 Ohm of driver, whose drop shrinks with the current. Dimmest, bounding VF by its
  3.1 V maximum (VF rises with IF, so it bounds every current below 5 mA; 3V3_D 3.284 V, R4 +1 %,
  50 Ohm driver): (3.284 - 3.1) / (1010 + 50) = 0.17 mA, at least 2.4 mcd, faint but lit;
  brightest (3.346 V, no driver drop, the 2.6 V minimum less 0.2 V, R4 -1 %): 0.946 V / 990 Ohm =
  0.96 mA, at most 33 mcd.
"""

load(
    "./passives.zen",
    "C_100N_0402",
    "LED_BLUE_0603",
    "LED_RED_0603",
    "R_10K_0402",
    "R_10_1206",
    "R_220_0402",
    "R_1K_0402",
)

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Led = Module("@stdlib/generics/Led.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
AO3400A = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/aos/AO3400A/AO3400A.zen")
D1N4148WS = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/cj/1N4148WS/1N4148WS.zen")
DSHP04TJGER = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/kangshen/DSHP04TJGER/DSHP04TJGER.zen")
FUET_5025 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/fuet/FUET-5025/FUET-5025.zen")
GT_TC048B = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/g-switch/GT-TC048B-H025-L1/GT-TC048B-H025-L1.zen")
CT1515 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/chongtian/CT-1515UGRBC/CT-1515UGRBC.zen")

# Its own sheet in the board schematic (layout/main.kicad_sch).
Project(name="Peripherals", path="layout", layout=False)

# A signal port takes the name of the board net it carries (the firmware's pin label) wherever
# that name is an identifier, so its sheet pin and hierarchical label match the root's label:
# KiCad's ERC flags labels whose names differ only in case (similar_labels).
V3V3_D = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)

Button = io(Net)
Reset = io(Net)
Boot = io(Net)
Switch_0 = io(Net)
Switch_1 = io(Net)
Switch_2 = io(Net)
Switch_3 = io(Net)
Buzzer = io(Net)
LED_ARGB = io(Net)
LED_Blue = io(Net)

BUZZER_GATE = Net("BUZZER_GATE")
BUZZER_DRAIN = Net("BUZZER_DRAIN")
BUZZER_COIL = Net("BUZZER_COIL")
LED_CHAIN = Net("LED_CHAIN")
LED_BLUE_A = Net("LED_BLUE_A")
LED_RED_A = Net("LED_RED_A")

# Buttons and switches.
GT_TC048B(name="SW2", A=GND, B=Button)
Capacitor(name="C20", P1=GND, P2=Button, **C_100N_0402)
GT_TC048B(name="SW3", A=GND, B=Reset)
Capacitor(name="C21", P1=GND, P2=Reset, **C_100N_0402)
Resistor(name="R42", P1=GND, P2=Boot, **R_10K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C60", P1=Boot, P2=GND, **C_100N_0402)
DSHP04TJGER(
    name="SW1",
    S1_A=Switch_0,
    S2_A=Switch_1,
    S3_A=Switch_2,
    S4_A=Switch_3,
    S1_B=GND,
    S2_B=GND,
    S3_B=GND,
    S4_B=GND,
)

# Buzzer.
FUET_5025(name="BZ1", POS=V3V3_D, NEG=BUZZER_COIL)
Resistor(name="R3", P1=BUZZER_DRAIN, P2=BUZZER_COIL, **R_10_1206)
AO3400A(name="Q1", G=BUZZER_GATE, S=GND, D=BUZZER_DRAIN)
Resistor(name="R1", P1=BUZZER_GATE, P2=Buzzer, **R_220_0402)
Resistor(name="R2", P1=GND, P2=BUZZER_GATE, **R_10K_0402)
D1N4148WS(name="D3", A=BUZZER_COIL, K=V3V3_D)

# LEDs: the CT-1515's 3-7.5 V operating range holds 3V3_D's 3.284-3.346 V (DS13554 Table 6).
CT1515(name="D1", VDD=V3V3_D, GND=GND, DI=LED_ARGB, DO=LED_CHAIN)
CT1515(name="D2", VDD=V3V3_D, GND=GND, DI=LED_CHAIN, DO=NotConnected())
Capacitor(name="C19", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C18", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Resistor(name="R4", P1=LED_BLUE_A, P2=LED_Blue, **R_1K_0402)
Led(name="D4", A=LED_BLUE_A, K=GND, **LED_BLUE_0603)
Resistor(name="R5", P1=LED_RED_A, P2=V3V3_D, **R_1K_0402)
Led(name="D5", A=LED_RED_A, K=GND, **LED_RED_0603)
